psg:pBkRGfgyATxirfE9P8IhIK
    a mrs:Passage ;
    rdfs:label "The Battle of Badr"@en ;
    mrs:canonicalCitation "50 Stories (rev 7), Part 3, story 20" ;
    skos:notation 20 ;
    mrs:inWitness wit:SfERCK2TeJUtCZL9VuJnPH ;
    dct:isPartOf psg:0F5OSXadhRL2SJDckLGkOu ;
    crm:P67_refers_to ev:oPlPpUrWs3Ruu3vusLUPv0 ;
    crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "In Ramadan of 2 AH, 313 Muslims with two horses faced about 1,000 Quraysh. Before battle, the Prophet ﷺ consulted his Companions, and both Muhajirun and Ansar pledged to follow him even into the sea. He spent the night in supplication until his cloak fell from his shoulders. Allah sent angels in support, and Quraysh were defeated, losing seventy dead including Abu Jahl."@en ;
    mrs:coverageState mrs:cs_stub ;
    mrs:createdBy agt:99lfWZ9Al5KAc3YUZNakNh ;
    mrs:recordedAt "2026-10-15T00:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

